    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always felt like a bridge between abstract patterns and real-world logic for me—something I find both fascinating and grounding. Though my education stopped at upper secondary, it’s a subject I’ve occasionally revisited to sharpen problem-solving in fields like physics or economics. It’s not just numbers; it’s the language of understanding cause and effect. My introversion makes complex problems feel manageable when broken down into steps, though I’m still curious about its deeper connections beyond surface-level algebra.",
